.Dd September 24, 2026
.Dt RT 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm rt ,
.Nm remote
.Nd reach this Mac's terminal remotely over SSH
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l Op Ar dir
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl k Ar keyfile
.Op Fl n
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl w Op Ar dir
.Op Fl b
.Op Fl p
.Op Fl C Ar cmd
.Nm remote
.Op Ar same options
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
and
.Nm remote
are the same command.
.Nm
runs a password-protected SSH server for the current user and makes it
reachable from anywhere through the public SSH relay ssh-j.com and a
Cloudflare quick tunnel, so the Mac can be used like a VPS.
It asks for a password when it starts; the password is kept only as a
slow PBKDF2 hash in memory and is gone when
.Nm
exits.
.Pp
Interactive shells
.Pq Li ssh host ,
single commands
.Pq Li ssh host 'cmd' ,
and SSH connection sharing
.Pq Cm ControlMaster
all work, so an agent can reuse a connection you logged into once without
knowing the password.
Agent forwarding and X11 forwarding are not supported, and forwarding is
refused unless
.Fl b
is given, which allows only a loopback reverse forward (see below).
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l Op Ar dir
Sandbox every session to
.Ar dir ,
or the current directory if none is given.
Sessions can read and write
.Ar dir ,
can run the Mac's installed tools, and cannot read the rest of the home
directory or write anywhere else except temporary directories.
They get a separate home directory,
.Pa ~/.local/state/rt/home ,
and cannot use the login keychain, open applications or send Apple Events.
.It Fl h
Also publish a web page for phones and browsers, behind the same password.
Its panel can hibernate and wake
.Nm ,
change the directory new sessions start in, and close sessions.
While hibernating, every open session is closed and new connections are
refused.
Its terminal runs a shell in the browser, with a row of Esc, Tab, Ctrl and
arrow keys on touch screens.
The shell keeps running for 15 minutes after the page disconnects, as it does
when a phone locks or switches apps, and the page reattaches to it.
.It Fl k Ar keyfile
Also require one of the public keys in
.Ar keyfile
(one key per line, in
.Pa authorized_keys
format without options).
The key is checked first, then the password.
.It Fl n
Do not connect to the relay or start a tunnel; listen on 127.0.0.1 only.
.It Fl c
When a session disconnects, send the client a script that removes traces of
the tunnel: the
.Pa known_hosts
entries for ssh-j.com and the relay name, the connection-sharing sockets, and
the matching shell-history lines.
Both a POSIX version (Linux, macOS, WSL) and a Windows PowerShell version are
sent, so the client can run whichever fits.
.It Fl w Op Ar dir
Also append every log line to
.Pa dir/rt.log ,
or
.Pa rt.log
in the current directory if none is given.
The file holds the same messages
.Nm
prints to its terminal, with a full date on each line, and is opened in append
mode so earlier runs are kept.
This is independent of
.Fl l ;
each option takes its own directory.
.It Fl b
Bidirectional.
Normally a session can only run commands on the Mac.
With
.Fl b ,
a client that joins with a reverse forward
.Pq Li ssh -R 127.0.0.1:0:127.0.0.1:22 ...
can be reached back from inside the session with the
.Ic peer
command, so one session drives both machines:
plain commands run on the Mac, and
.Ic peer Ar cmd
runs
.Ar cmd
on the client.
This is meant for agents that log in to the Mac and also need to act on the
machine they came from.
.Pp
.Ic peer
connects to the client's own sshd through the reverse tunnel, so the client
must accept that login.
It logs in as the name the client used to join
.Pq the value of Ev RT_PEER_USER , No which defaults to that name ,
so a key the client already trusts makes
.Ic peer
passwordless; otherwise the client's password is asked.
Override the login by setting
.Ev RT_PEER_USER
before
.Ic peer .
Only loopback forwards are accepted, and only with
.Fl b ;
without it all forwarding is refused, as usual.
.It Fl p
Persist with the lid closed.
.Nm
always runs
.Xr caffeinate 8
so the Mac stays awake while it runs, but macOS still sleeps when the lid
is shut.
.Fl p
also runs
.Li sudo pmset -a disablesleep 1
at startup, which needs the sudo password once, and undoes it
.Pq Li disablesleep 0
when
.Nm
exits normally.
If lid-closed sleep was already disabled,
.Nm
leaves it untouched.
.It Fl C Ar cmd
Run
.Ar cmd
instead of a login shell when a client asks for an interactive shell, so a
connection drops straight into
.Ar cmd .
Single commands
.Pq Li ssh host 'cmd'
are unaffected.
This is how
.Xr rtc 1
starts Claude Code on connect.
.El
.Pp
Without
.Fl l ,
sessions have the user's full access and start in the current directory.
.Sh CONNECTING
.Nm
checks each route end to end before it prints the command for it.
.Pp
The relay route needs nothing but
.Xr ssh 1
on the other computer:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ssh -J NAME@ssh-j.com mac
.Ed
.Pp
.Ar NAME
is
.Ql rt-
and 8 random letters and digits without look-alikes, created on the first
run and kept, so the command stays the same.
If ssh reports
.Dq administratively prohibited ,
the name was mistyped or
.Nm
is not running.
The Mac keeps an outgoing SSH connection to ssh-j.com open and reconnects if
it drops.
The relay only forwards the session, which stays encrypted between the two
computers; the first connection asks to trust ssh-j.com's key and this Mac's,
whose fingerprint
.Nm
prints.
ssh-j.com listens on port 22 only.
.Pp
If a network blocks port 22, the Cloudflare route goes over HTTPS but needs
.Xr cloudflared 1
on the other computer:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ssh -o "ProxyCommand=cloudflared access ssh --hostname %h" HOST
.Ed
.Pp
Quick tunnel host names change every time
.Nm
starts.
Without cloudflared on the Mac only the relay runs, and
.Fl h
is unavailable.
Both commands are shown in the phone panel with a copy button, and
.Nm
prints an
.Pa ~/.ssh/config
entry with connection sharing for the relay route.
.Pp
To give Claude Code a token inside a session, send it from the client:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ssh -o SendEnv=CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN ...
.Ed
.Pp
Only
.Ev LANG ,
.Ev LC_* ,
.Ev COLORTERM ,
.Ev CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
and
.Ev ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
are accepted from the client.
.Sh SECURITY
Each connection runs in its own process, started fresh with
.Xr execv 2
so it never holds the password hash.
A separate supervisor process checks passwords, keeps the hibernation state
and the panel, and can kill any session.
.Pp
After three wrong passwords in a row, from SSH or the panel together, each
further attempt must wait 1, 2, 4 ... up to 60 seconds; after ten,
.Nm
refuses all logins for 15 minutes.
Every login, logout and wrong password is logged to the terminal running
.Nm ,
and to
.Pa rt.log
as well when
.Fl w
is given.
.Pp
The panel's login cookie is HttpOnly, Secure and SameSite=Strict, and every
API request must carry a custom header, so other sites cannot act on it.
.Sh SLEEP
.Nm
runs
.Xr caffeinate 8
so the Mac stays awake while it runs, including with the screen locked.
With the lid closed macOS still sleeps unless
.Fl p
is given, which runs
.Li sudo pmset -a disablesleep 1
for you and undoes it on exit
.Pq Li 0 No undoes it by hand ;
without
.Fl p ,
.Nm
says so at startup.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.local/state/rt/host_ed25519
SSH host key, created on first run.
Its fingerprint is printed at startup; compare it the first time you connect.
.It Pa ~/.local/state/rt/home
Home directory for sandboxed sessions.
.It Pa ~/.local/state/rt/relay_name
The relay name; delete it to get a new join command.
Every
.Nm
on the Mac uses it, so only the first one running gets the relay route;
the others say so and retry every 30 seconds.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cloudflared 1 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5 ,
.Xr caffeinate 8
